{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/443892-kindred-of-the-east-translation-the-devil-tigers","id":443892,"title":"Kindred of the East Translation: The Devil Tigers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T01:29:03-07:00","id":443892,"title":"Kindred of the East Translation: The Devil Tigers","content":"The Triumphant Howl of the Devil Tiger<br /> <br /> \u201cYou thought when you got out of Cambodia, you were safe. Three hundred women, you sent to death. Pol Pot didn\u2019t care that your justification was flimsy, or that you just sent them away to die because you thought they were prettier then you. Tonight, the hungry ghosts feed, and we shall see how pretty you look once they finish.\u201d<br /> <br /> Like the Lancea Et Sanctum, the Devil Tigers believe they are fully damned. They will descend to Naraka, the lowest path of reincarnation in Buddhist lore , there they will suffer for untold millennia depending on the sums of their sins.<br /> <br /> But unlike the Hell of the Christians, Naraka doesn\u2019t last forever.<br /> <br /> The Devil Tigers believe the Kindred curse is a sacred brand, a mark placed on them by Yama (Sometimes called Emna-O), a divinely mandated duty. The world is full of sinners and monsters, those destined for Naraka when they die. And it\u2019s the Devil Tiger\u2019s duty to speed them on their way, before the depraved and wicked drag others down with them.<br /> <br /> In doing so, they shorten their own durance in Naraka. If they fulfill their duties, Yama will free them from Hell, and when they pass from this existence, they will be reborn based on the Karma they have built up cleansing the world of evil and wickendness. Yama damned them not out of a desire to see them suffer, but has motivation to ensure they fulfill their duties. Those so cursed consider their damnation an exalted state, something to be celebrated has they were chosen by the gods for a sacred duty.<br /> <br /> But that doesn\u2019t mean they want to go to hell, even if they\u2019ll get out eventually. Every wicked soul consigned to its rightful place in hell buys time off of the karmic debt Yama imposed on them, and it\u2019s said that some Elder Devil Tigers will be reborn in even higher realms, has Ashura or even Deva (Not to be confused with the clan, and younger Daeva who try to claim some authority over the Devil Tigers with this association do not tend to see their next sunset)<br /> But they do not interfere with the pure of heart; their duty is to purge the world of the wicked, not to terrify people back to the church. They simply don\u2019t get involved with things that are pure because they themselves are impure. The more purist Devil Tigers refuse to go anywhere near children, religious mortals, or anybody who lives a virtuous life, lest their own cursed state negatively affect the individuals Karma. Even younger Devils avoid schools and churches when they can.<br /> <br /> Devil Tigers take pleasure in killings that teach a lesson. A murderer is killed with his own knife, so when he plunges into Naraka and goes before Yama, he will tell the Judge of the Dead what occurred, and what he learned from his death. They think Yama has a peculiar sense of humor and irony, and smiles on actions that teach cruel and painful lessons to their victims. After all, Hell may last a very long time, but every soul leaves Naraka eventually, and lessons learned in one life may carry on to the next.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tools of the trade<br /> The Devil Tigers consider the unclean \u201cTheir Territory\u201d. Ghosts, demons, wicked spirits, and inhuman mortals are all acceptable tools with which to purge the world of evil. Has such, Bloodlines with an affinity for such are highly valued.<br /> <br /> They also have an unusual form of Cruac, which is based on Asian mythology and culture. Yama is a powerful God, after all, and by claiming his divine mandate, they may exploit the powers of other, lesser Gods to complete their duties. Most Devil Tigers are careful with their Cruac, nobody wants to enter Yama\u2019s court at the end of their Requiem to find him speaking with a God who\u2019s power they drew on a few times too many for frivolous reasons.<br /> Demon summoning (WoD: Inferno) is also not uncommon. Infernal Pacts are not considered to harm the Vampire\u2019s Karma, so long as they use it to fulfill their duties and control the demon effectively. It is said Yama laughs loudest when a Devil Tiger calls up a vile spirit, and sends it on a duty that ends with the spirit and its target destroyed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sects and Factions<br /> <br /> The Devil Tigers exist all over Asia, but Asia is made of dozens, if not hundreds of countries, all with their own cultures, subcultures, faiths and ideologies. Only a fool assumes a Chinese Devil Tiger, an Indian Devil Tiger, and a Japanese Devil Tiger are going to do things exactly the same way. There are even a few Devil Tigers in port cities on the West Coast of the United States.<br /> <br /> The Kami\u2019s Scalpel: One of the larger sects of the Devil Tigers, these Tigers see pollution, global warming, and other environmental issues has being evidence that Naraka is \u201cLeaking\u201d into the Human Realm. They target those greedy individuals who pollute and cause damage to the environment through either neglect, or callous greed. At their best, they\u2019re environmentalists determined to show these criminals the error of their ways.<br /> <br /> At their worst, they brutally slaughter people they catch throwing Mc Donalds wrappers out on the freeway because the next rest stop is 50 miles away and commit violent acts of ecoterrorism. All Devil Tigers kill, but these Tigers tend to be more pragmatic about who they murder. It\u2019s easier to convince an executive to be a little more ethical then it is to kill him, and his next four or five replacements until someone gets the message. (Though their \u2018convincing\u2019 tends to involve lots of Nightmare or Dominate, or if that doesn\u2019t work, ghosts and demons).<br /> <br /> <br /> Kannon\u2019s Thousand Hands: A Boddhisvatha with a thousand arms and eleven heads to hear the cries of the multitudes and aid the same, this sect of Devil Tigers targets those who commit sexual crimes, human trafficking, and anything that directly causes abject human misery.<br /> Their wrath is legendary, with those who rape and ruin lives with impunity being struck down with horrible Cruac-Conjured plagues that rot their flesh from the outside in, leaving them little better then walking canvases of syphilis and rot. A number of Morbus Vampires have managed to make some gains in this covenant by using their powers over disease to inflict sinners with the most brutal plagues they can imagine.<br /> <br /> That said, every so often the plagues DO spread, and the Devil Tigers, in their haste to deliver swift and brutal justice, sometimes target the wrong individual. Maybe they killed someone who had the same name has a human trafficker? Maybe this fellow\u2019s girlfriend lied about the rape? In their haste to \u201chelp\u201d they sometimes do more harm than good, and Yama is nothing if not a just god, and his anger is swiftly riled by being sent innocent souls who died before their time at the hands of his servants.<br /> <br /> Durga\u2019s Tigers (Sometimes Kali\u2019s Tigers): A mostly Indian sect, arising out of the British Raj, and claiming a number of Rakshasha Nosferatu, this sect is devoted to new and creative ways to murder murderers. They practice Murder has if it were an art, finding new and creative ways to punish the wicked, and constantly driving their peers to new bloody heights in their quest to deliver Yama\u2019s justice.<br /> <br /> Tigers of Durga watch subjects carefully, attempting to ascertain beyond any reasonable doubt that their subject is guilty and must die. Tigers of Kali are less discriminating, with low humanity Kindred usually being dubbed has \u201cThirsting like Kali\u201d, and slaughtering murderers with cruel and reckless abandon, sometimes even slaughtering those they think are likely to commit murders.<br /> <br /> Those Tigers of Kali who go too far are usually hunted down by the Tigers of Durga, and sent to explain their actions to Yama before their actions poke too many holes in the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Tiger Sorcery: Devil Tiger Cruac<br /> Like the Cruac of the Circle of the Crone, Tiger Cruac puts the usual restrictions on ones humanity. This is seen has the natural result of drawing on the spiritual essence of Hell. If you use the power of devils, you become more like a devil. However Yama has no use for Dragur, and those who lose too much humanity too fast are usually put to death before they harm their karma and the karma of others any more.<br /> <br /> Unlike \u201cmainstream\u201d Cruac, Tiger Cruac CAN effect Spirits and Ghosts. However, they may only affect ethereal beings that are somehow corrupt or wicked. Mechanically, this means any Spirit that represents a malign or \u201cEvil\u201d concept (Murder, rape, blood, toxic waste) and any ghost with a morality of three or less is subject to Cruac rituals. Anything that does not fit this qualification is unable to be effected by Cruac per the usual rituals. Tiger Cruac has a few unique rituals specifically geared towards summoning and commanding wicked spirits, hungry ghosts, and Inferno Demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Views from without<br /> <br /> Lancea Et Sanctum: Heretics who worship a thousand pagan gods, the only thing that disgusts me more than their blasphemy is how much they remind me of my youth\u2026<br /> <br /> Circle of the Crone: They don\u2019t honor the Goddess, they crave destruction and mayhem, and they worship an overbearing Male divinity? The only good thing about them is that when they clear the fields, we can plant what we will.<br /> <br /> Invictus: You\u2019re telling me a six foot tall green tiger belching hellfire with bone spurs jutting out of its body burned down your Manor? Of all the reasons to be late to a meeting, that one takes the cake.<br /> <br /> Carthians: Yeah man! Fight the power, fight the\u2026wait, what are you looking at me like that fo-<br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul: Slaves to demons and devils, who accept their condition with holy zeal. We can learn nothing from them.<br /> <br /> Werewolves: Me and the pack heard about this wound that opened up after Fukushima hit. We got down there, and there was this toxin spirit screaming and screaming, and when we got a little closer we saw that something was wriggling around in its gut. Next thing we know, this man EXPLODES out of their stomach, ripping its guts out with claws that rivaled ours, and broke its back over its knee. It took one look at us, nodded, and ran off into the night. We couldn\u2019t track it, the whole place stank of rot and waste, but it cleared things up enough we\u2019ve been able to shrink the wound a great deal.<br /> My only question is did that thing know we were coming? Or was that just a happy coincidence?<br /> <br /> Mages: From what I\u2019ve heard of these \u201cDevil Tigers\u201d their ideology seems to be rather similar to the average Mastigos\u2019s view of Pandaemonium. And they say the Gods where forced out of the Supernal by the Exarchs. Which begs the question; what exactly are these demon-summoning vampires worshipping?<br /> <br /> Demons (God Machine): It\u2019s all well and good until they figure out that your newest Cover had been implicated in a gang rape in college, and they decide to bring down the hammer. I went loud, thrashed them, and I\u2019ve been stuck flipping burgers for the last six months. At least I had a backup cover, but I\u2019m going to miss that limo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1645,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","user":"Autochthon","date":". 03-16-2015, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T02:29:52-07:00","id":443950,"title":"","content":"A minor nitpick here- the books don't say that blood magic can't affect ephemerals, but that it doesn't extend to dealing with the otherworlds. <br /> <br /> So I believe the intent was that luring a ghost to you is fine, teleporting to the underworld is not, crones have to find a gate like every other tourist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T03:00:59-07:00","id":443967,"title":"","content":"I thought Blood and Smoke and the Blood Sorcery book said they couldn't futz with such?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T03:46:27-07:00","id":443989,"title":"","content":"Nope, they can alright as long as the ghost/spirit/whatever is in twilight. They can summon, bind, control, etc, them just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}